  "note": "Expected outputs worked out by hand from AC_PosControl.cpp, AC_P_2D/AC_P_1D/AC_PID_2D/AC_PID_Basic/AC_PID.cpp and AP_Math/control.cpp; every value is exact in binary32 except the four atanf results (pc_pitch and pc_lean_angle at steps 1 and 2, macOS libm, ardupilot/modules/position/hand-checked-libm.c, which prints them). Parameters: Copter's PSC_ defaults except all PID filters off (FLTE = FLTD = FLTT = 0, so calc_lowpass_alpha_dt returns 1 and every filter passes its input), PSC_ANGLE_MAX 0 (use ATC_ANGLE_MAX), dt = 1/256 s, hover throttle 0.5, ATC_ANGLE_MAX 45 deg (0.7853982 rad, tanf = 1 exactly in binary32, so the NE accel limit is 9.80665), altitude-hold lean limit 90 deg. Vehicle: at (0, 0, -10) m, at rest, measuring 1 g (accel_ef.z = -9.80665), level, yaw 0 (cos 1, sin 0). STEP 0 (hover at the target): update_estimates, NE_init_controller, D_init_controller, NE_update_controller, D_update_controller. The scheduler tick is 1 and the stored ticks are 0, so NE_is_active() is true inside NE_init_controller and the lean-angle conversion is skipped: the accel target stays 0 (zeroed object). NE_init: targets = estimate, NE vel PID integrator set to 0 - 0 * FF = 0. D_init: estimated accel D = -9.80665 + 9.80665 = 0, accel target 0, accel PID integrator -(0.5 - 0.5) - 0.05 * 0 - 0 * 0 = -0, then +0 after update_i adds 0. NE update: P error 0, sqrt_controller(0) = 0, velocity target 0, velocity PID (filter reset) error 0, output 0; not limited (limit vector 0); accel_NE_mss_to_lean_angles: forward accel 0, pitch = atanf(-0 / g) = -0 (0x80000000), roll = atanf(0) = 0; desired speed 0, so yaw = the attitude target's yaw 0 and yaw rate 0. D update: position error 0, velocity target 0, velocity PID 0 (I gain 0 keeps its integrator 0), accel target 0, accel PID error 0 - 0 = 0, P = D = I = FF = 0, so thrust_d = 0 + 0 - 0.5 and set_throttle_out(0.5, true, 2): level thrust vector (0, 0, -9.80665), throttle_in = hover = 0.5. Control ratio 2 + dt * 0.1 * 0.5 constrained to 2, reported constrained to 1. Stopping points: speed 0, so (0, 0); vertical inv_sqrt_controller(0, 1, 2.5) = 0, so -10. Limits are the constructor's (5, 2.5, 1.5 m/s; 1, 2.5 m/s/s; jerk 5, 5). STEP 1 (a 0.125 m step north): guidance hands set_pos_vel_accel_NED_m((0.125, 0, -10), 0, 0) and terrain 0. NE update: position target = desired + offset 0 = 0.125; AC_P_2D error (0.125, 0), no error limit (correction limits never set: _error_max = _D1_max = 0), sqrt_controller with second-order limit 0 is linear: 0.125 * P 1 = 0.125, so velocity target (0.125, 0) (scalers 1, desired velocity 0). AC_PID_2D: error 0 + (0.125 - 0) * 1 = 0.125; derivative (0.125 - 0) / (1/256) = 32, filtered 32; I: 0 + 0.125 * 1 * (1/256) = 1/2048 (limit vector 0: no anti-windup); output = 0.125 * 2 + 1/2048 + 32 * 0.25 + 0.125 * 0 = 8.25048828125 m/s/s north, below the limit 9.80665, so not limited: thrust (8.25048828125, 0, -9.80665), pitch target atanf(-8.25048828125 / 9.80665) = 0xbf330de3 (-0.6994 rad, nose down to accelerate north), roll atanf(0) = 0, tilt observer 0x3f330de3. Vertical unchanged: throttle_in 0.5. STEP 2 (target held): velocity target again 0.125, error 0.125 + (0.125 - 0.125) = 0.125, derivative 0 (filtered: 32 + (0 - 32) * 1 = 0), I = 1/2048 + 1/2048 = 1/1024, output 0.25 + 1/1024 + 0 = 0.2509765625: the derivative kick of step 1 is gone; pitch atanf(-0.2509765625 / 9.80665) = 0xbcd19b9f. The vehicle has not moved (the estimate is an input), so the position error stays 0.125. Composition: outputs pc_vel_max_ne/up/down, pc_accel_max_ne/d renamed pc_ne_max_speed, pc_max_speed_up/down, pc_ne_max_accel, pc_d_max_accel; the guidance hand-over inputs tgt_* (added) are false/0. Since the composition a tgt_valid with NED targets runs NE_update_controller (AC_WPNav::update_wpnav's own call): the case's cmd_position_NE_update_controller is false at the 2 steps with tgt_valid (the one NE update per tick the expected outputs were worked for). Inputs added later (32: the `_seq` call-order fields and signals) are 0/false: fixed order, the steps are unchanged. Output pc_throttle_seq (added) is 0: not sequenced. Estimator names (since the composition with the real estimator stage): est_pos_ne_valid and est_pos_d_valid (equal here) are est_pos_ok; est_vel_valid est_vel_ok; est_vert_pos_rate_d/_valid est_pos_rate_d/_ok; est_accel_ef_d est_accel_ef_z; est_control_gain_scaler_xy/z est_gain_scaler_xy/z. Inputs cmd_attitude_set_throttle_out, _throttle_in, _seq (added with the same-tick throttle rule) are false, 0, 0: the steps are unchanged; outputs re-recorded, all earlier fields bit-identical. Inputs added with the loiter stage (the 25 lt_ hand-over ports) are false/0: no loiter call; every previously recorded output field came out bit-identical when this file was regenerated (2026-11-18).",
